      },
      "type": "sidebar"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Dwarf Heritages"
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 126,
        "endLine": 126,
        "startOffset": 3844,
        "endOffset": 3861
      },
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Dwarves take great pride in the resilience of their bloodlines. Choose one of the following dwarven heritages at 1st level."
        }
      ],
      "indent": "none",
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 128,
        "endLine": 129,
        "startOffset": 3863,
        "endOffset": 3986
      },
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Ancient-Blooded Dwarf"
        }
      ],
      "level": 2,
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "endLine": 131,
        "startOffset": 3988,
        "endOffset": 4012
      },
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Dwarven heroes of old could shrug off their enemies’ magic, and some of that resistance manifests in you. You gain the Call on Ancient Blood reaction."
        }
      ],
      "indent": "none",
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "endLine": 134,
        "startOffset": 4014,
        "endOffset": 4164
      },
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Call on Ancient Blood"
            }
          ],
          "kind": "strong"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "kind": "action",
          "symbol": ":r:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Trigger"
            }
          ],
          "kind": "strong"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " You attempt a saving throw against a magical effect, but you haven’t rolled yet; "
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Effect"
            }
          ],
          "kind": "strong"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " Your ancestors’ innate resistance to magic surges before slowly ebbing down. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws on the triggering save and other saves against magical effects until the end of this turn."
        }
      ],
      "indent": "first-line",
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 136,
        "endLine": 140,
        "startOffset": 4166,
        "endOffset": 4517
      },
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Death Warden Dwarf"
        }
      ],
      "level": 2,
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 142,
        "endLine": 142,
        "startOffset": 4519,
        "endOffset": 4540
      },
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Your ancestors were tomb guardians, and their power to ward off death passed on to you. If you roll a success on a saving throw against an effect that has the void trait or was created by an undead creature, you get a critical success instead."
        }
      ],
      "indent": "none",
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 144,
        "endLine": 146,
        "startOffset": 4542,
        "endOffset": 4785
      },
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Forge Dwarf"
        }
      ],
      "level": 2,
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "endLine": 148,
        "startOffset": 4787,
        "endOffset": 4801
      },
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "You have a remarkable adaptation to hot environments. This grants you fire resistance equal to half your level (minimum 1), and you treat environmental heat effects as if they were one step less extreme (incredible heat becomes extreme, extreme heat becomes severe, and so on)."
        }
      ],
      "indent": "none",
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 150,
        "endLine": 153,
        "startOffset": 4803,
        "endOffset": 5080
      },
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Rock Dwarf"
        }
      ],
      "level": 2,
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 155,
        "endLine": 155,
        "startOffset": 5082,
        "endOffset": 5095
      },
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Your ancestors lived and worked among the ancient stones of the mountains or the depths of the earth. This makes you solid as a rock when you plant your feet. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude or Reflex DC against attempts to Reposition, Shove, or Trip you. This bonus also applies to saving throws against spells or effects that attempt to force you to move or knock you prone."
        }
      ],
      "indent": "none",
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 157,
        "endLine": 161,
        "startOffset": 5097,
        "endOffset": 5492
      },
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "In addition, if any effect would force you to move 10 feet or more, you are moved only half the distance."
        }
      ],
      "indent": "first-line",
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 163,
        "endLine": 164,
        "startOffset": 5494,
        "endOffset": 5599
      },
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Strong-Blooded Dwarf"
        }
      ],
      "level": 2,
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 166,
        "endLine": 166,
        "startOffset": 5601,
        "endOffset": 5624
      },
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Your blood runs hearty and strong, and you can shake off toxins. You gain poison resistance equal to half your level (minimum 1), and each of your successful saving throws against a poison affliction reduces its stage by 2, or by 1 for a virulent poison. Each critical success against an ongoing poison reduces its stage by 3, or by 2 for a virulent poison."
        }
      ],
      "indent": "none",
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 168,
        "endLine": 172,
        "startOffset": 5626,
        "endOffset": 5983
      },
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Ancestry Feats"
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "endLine": 174,
        "startOffset": 5985,
        "endOffset": 6001
      },
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "At 1st level, you gain one ancestry feat, and you gain an additional ancestry feat every 4 levels thereafter (at 5th, 9th, 13th, and 17th level). As a dwarf, you select from among the following ancestry feats."
        }
      ],
      "indent": "none",
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "endLine": 178,
        "startOffset": 6003,
        "endOffset": 6212
      },
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "1ST LEVEL"
        }
      ],
      "level": 4,
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 180,
        "endLine": 180,
        "startOffset": 6214,
        "endOffset": 6228
      },
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "You are naturally calm and collected in the face of imminent danger. At the end of your turn, reduce your frightened condition by 2 instead of 1."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "none",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 188,
            "endLine": 189,
            "startOffset": 6278,
            "endOffset": 6423
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "DWARVEN DOUGHTINESS"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 182,
        "endLine": 190,
        "startOffset": 6230,
        "endOffset": 6425
      },
      "subtitle": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "FEAT 1"
        }
      ],
      "traits": [
        "Dwarf"
      ],
      "type": "item"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "You eagerly absorbed the old stories and traditions of your ancestors, your gods, and your people, studying subjects and techniques passed down for generation upon generation. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Crafting and Religion. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "none",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 198,
            "endLine": 202,
            "startOffset": 6468,
            "endOffset": 6872
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "You also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Dwarf Lore."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "first-line",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 204,
            "endLine": 204,
            "startOffset": 6874,
            "endOffset": 6936
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "DWARVEN LORE"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "endLine": 205,
        "startOffset": 6427,
        "endOffset": 6938
      },
      "subtitle": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "FEAT 1"
        }
      ],
      "traits": [
        "Dwarf"
      ],
      "type": "item"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Your kin have instilled in you an affinity for hard-hitting weapons, and you prefer these to more elegant arms. You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the dwarf trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the dwarf trait plus the battle axe, pick, and warhammer—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "none",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 213,
            "endLine": 218,
            "startOffset": 6995,
            "endOffset": 7417
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "At 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "first-line",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 220,
            "endLine": 221,
            "startOffset": 7419,
            "endOffset": 7535
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "DWARVEN WEAPON FAMILIARITY"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 207,
        "endLine": 222,
        "startOffset": 6940,
        "endOffset": 7537
      },
      "subtitle": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "FEAT 1"
        }
      ],
      "traits": [
        "Dwarf"
      ],
      "type": "item"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Dwarves have a long history fighting common foes, and you’ve mastered the ancient tactics to better face these enemies. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to damage with weapons and unarmed attacks against creatures with the giant, goblin, hryngar, or orc trait. If your attack would deal more than one weapon die of damage (as is common at higher levels than 1st), the bonus is equal to the number of weapon dice or unarmed attack dice."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "none",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 230,
            "endLine": 235,
            "startOffset": 7585,
            "endOffset": 8020
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "In addition, if any creature critically succeeds at an attack against you and deals damage to you, you gain your bonus to damage against that creature for 1 minute regardless of whether it has the chosen trait."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "first-line",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 237,
            "endLine": 239,
            "startOffset": 8022,
            "endOffset": 8232
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "hr",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 241,
            "endLine": 241,
            "startOffset": 8234,
            "endOffset": 8235
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "text": "Special"
                }
              ],
              "kind": "strong"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": " Your GM can add appropriate creature traits to the ancestral foes list if your character is from a community that commonly fights other types of enemies."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "hanging",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 243,
            "endLine": 244,
            "startOffset": 8237,
            "endOffset": 8402
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "MOUNTAIN STRATEGY"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "endLine": 245,
        "startOffset": 7539,
        "endOffset": 8404
      },
      "subtitle": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "FEAT 1"
        }
      ],
      "traits": [
        "Dwarf"
      ],
      "type": "item"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Your innate connection to stone makes you adept at moving across uneven surfaces. You can ignore difficult terrain caused by stone (such as rubble or gravel) and uneven ground made of stone and earth. In addition, when you use the Acrobatics skill to Balance on narrow surfaces or uneven ground made of stone or earth, you aren’t off-guard, and when you roll a success at one of these Acrobatics checks, you get a critical success instead."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "none",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 253,
            "endLine": 258,
            "startOffset": 8446,
            "endOffset": 8885
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "ROCK RUNNER"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 247,
        "endLine": 259,
        "startOffset": 8406,
        "endOffset": 8887
      },
      "subtitle": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "FEAT 1"
        }
      ],
      "traits": [
        "Dwarf"
      ],
      "type": "item"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "You understand the intricacies of stonework. You become trained in Crafting. If you’re already trained in Crafting, you instead gain the Specialty Crafting skill feat for stonemasonry."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "none",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 267,
            "endLine": 269,
            "startOffset": 8934,
            "endOffset": 9118
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "You also gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to notice unusual stonework. This bonus applies to checks to discover mechanical traps made of stone or hidden within stone."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "first-line",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 271,
            "endLine": 273,
            "startOffset": 9120,
            "endOffset": 9303
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "If you aren’t using the Seek action or searching, the GM automatically rolls a secret check for you to notice unusual stonework anyway. This check doesn’t gain your normal circumstance bonus."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "first-line",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 275,
            "endLine": 277,
            "startOffset": 9305,
            "endOffset": 9496
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "STONEMASON’S EYE"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 261,
        "endLine": 278,
        "startOffset": 8889,
        "endOffset": 9498
      },
      "subtitle": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "FEAT 1"
        }
      ],
      "traits": [
        "Dwarf"
      ],
      "type": "item"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "You’ve learned techniques first devised by your ancestors during their ancient wars, allowing you to comfortably wear massive suits of armor. Ignore the reduction to your Speed from any armor you wear."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "none",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 286,
            "endLine": 288,
            "startOffset": 9544,
            "endOffset": 9745
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "In addition, any time you’re taking a penalty to your Speed for some other reason (such as from the encumbered condition or from a spell), deduct 5 feet from the penalty. For example, the encumbered condition normally gives a –10-foot penalty to Speed, but this feat would reduce it to a –5-foot penalty. If your Speed is taking multiple penalties, pick only one penalty to reduce."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "first-line",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 290,
            "endLine": 294,
            "startOffset": 9747,
            "endOffset": 10128
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "UNBURDENED IRON"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 280,
        "endLine": 295,
        "startOffset": 9500,
        "endOffset": 10130
      },
      "subtitle": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "FEAT 1"
        }
      ],
      "traits": [
        "Dwarf"
      ],
      "type": "item"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "5TH LEVEL"
        }
      ],
      "level": 4,
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 297,
        "endLine": 297,
        "startOffset": 10132,
        "endOffset": 10146
      },
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "action": ":aa:",
      "content": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "text": "Prerequisites"
                }
              ],
              "kind": "strong"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": " Rock Runner"
            }
          ],
          "indent": "hanging",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 305,
            "endLine": 305,
            "startOffset": 10194,
            "endOffset": 10223
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "hr",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 307,
            "endLine": 307,
            "startOffset": 10225,
            "endOffset": 10226
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Your dwarven build allows you to push foes around, just like a mighty boulder tumbles through a subterranean cavern. Take a Step into the square of a foe that is your size or smaller, and the foe must move into the empty space directly behind it. The foe must move even if doing so places it in harm’s way. The foe can attempt a Fortitude saving throw against your Athletics DC to block your Step. If the foe attempts this saving throw, it takes bludgeoning damage equal to your level plus your Strength modifier unless it critically succeeds."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "none",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 309,
            "endLine": 315,
            "startOffset": 10228,
            "endOffset": 10771
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "If the foe can’t move into an empty space (if it is surrounded by solid objects or other creatures, for example), your Boulder Roll has no effect."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "first-line",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 317,
            "endLine": 318,
            "startOffset": 10773,
            "endOffset": 10919
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "BOULDER ROLL"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 299,
        "endLine": 319,
        "startOffset": 10148,
        "endOffset": 10921
      },
      "subtitle": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "FEAT 5"
        }
      ],
      "traits": [
        "Dwarf"
      ],
      "type": "item"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "text": "Prerequisites"
                }
              ],
              "kind": "strong"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": " darkvision"
            }
          ],
          "indent": "hanging",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 327,
            "endLine": 327,
            "startOffset": 10969,
            "endOffset": 10997
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "hr",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 329,
            "endLine": 329,
            "startOffset": 10999,
            "endOffset": 11000
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Using ancient dwarven methods developed to fight enemies wielding magical darkness, you’ve honed your darkvision and sworn not to use such magic yourself. You gain greater darkvision, enabling you to see through magical darkness even if it normally hampers darkvision (such as the darkness created by a 4th-rank "
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "text": "darkness"
                }
              ],
              "kind": "em"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": " spell). You can’t cast spells with the darkness trait, use item activations with the darkness trait, or use any other ability with the darkness trait."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "none",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 331,
            "endLine": 337,
            "startOffset": 11002,
            "endOffset": 11475
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "DEFY THE DARKNESS"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "endLine": 338,
        "startOffset": 10923,
        "endOffset": 11477
      },
      "subtitle": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "FEAT 5"
        }
      ],
      "traits": [
        "Dwarf"
      ],
      "type": "item"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "text": "Prerequisites"
                }
              ],
              "kind": "strong"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": " expert in Crafting"
            }
          ],
          "indent": "hanging",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 346,
            "endLine": 346,
            "startOffset": 11529,
            "endOffset": 11565
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "hr",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 348,
            "endLine": 348,
            "startOffset": 11567,
            "endOffset": 11568
          }
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "You can use your knowledge of engineering and metalwork to temporarily strengthen thick objects and structures. By spending 1 hour working on an item, you can give it a +1 circumstance bonus to its Hardness for 24 hours. If you’re a master in Crafting, the bonus is +2, and if you’re legendary, the bonus is +3. You can reinforce a portion of a structure, though 1 hour usually reinforces only a door, a few windows, or another section that fits within a 10-foot cube."
            }
          ],
          "indent": "none",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "origin": {
            "startLine": 350,
            "endLine": 355,
            "startOffset": 11570,
            "endOffset": 12038
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "DWARVEN REINFORCEMENT"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "startLine": 340,
        "endLine": 356,
        "startOffset": 11479,
        "endOffset": 12040
      },
      "subtitle": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "FEAT 5"
        }
      ],
      "traits": [
        "Dwarf"
      ],
      "type": "item"
    }
  ]
}
